  <Section {...S["column-visibility"]}>
        <p>
          Give a menu checkbox item <code>data-column</code> set to the
          <code>id</code> of a header cell in the table's first header row,
          and the item shows and hides that column. While the item is
          unchecked, the header cell and the column's cell in every body and
          footer row are hidden, and they leave the accessibility tree. A cell
          that spans several columns, such as a detail row's cell, stays. An
          item unchecked when the page loads starts its column hidden.
        </p>
        <p>
          The framework fires no event of its own. To keep the choice across
          visits, save it from the menu's <code>expressive:change</code>,
          which carries <code>{"{ item, checked }"}</code>, and render each
          item's <code>aria-checked</code> from what you saved. After changing
          <code>aria-checked</code> from script, or for a table rendered
          later, call <code>Expressive.DataTables.sync(wrapper)</code>. Name
          only header cells that span one column. Leave the row header column
          out of the menu, and under <code>sticky-column</code> the pinned
          columns too.
        </p>
        <div class="data-table-actions">
          <button type="button" class="button text menu-trigger" data-target="visibility-columns">Columns</button>
        </div>
        <div class="data-table">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr><th scope="col">Customer</th><th scope="col" id="visibility-status">Status</th><th scope="col">Region</th><th scope="col" id="visibility-total" class="numeric">Total</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
